            "explanation": "In pydantic/_internal/_typing_extra.py the vendored _type_convert helper builds a ForwardRef for string annotations using `ForwardRef(arg, is_argument=False, is_class=True)`. On Python 3.10 ForwardRef.__init__ does not accept `is_class`, which matches the reported TypeError when a model with a string forward-reference like `x: \"int\"` is defined.",
